  "result": "Perfect! All 108 tests pass (83 original + 25 new). I've successfully added line discount functionality to the invoicing system.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **Added `DISCOUNT_INVALID` error code** to `src/errors.js`\n\n2. **Updated `createInvoice()`** to accept `discountPercent` (0-100, can be decimal):\n   - Validates discount is a number between 0 and 100\n   - Stores discount on the line if provided\n   - Returns DISCOUNT_INVALID for invalid values\n\n3. **Updated `addLine()`** to accept and validate `discountPercent`:\n   - Same validation as createInvoice\n   - Updates discount on existing lines if provided\n\n4. **Created `lineDiscount(line)`** function:\n   - Calculates discount amount as: lineTotal \u00d7 discountPercent \u00f7 100\n   - Returns 0 if no discount\n   - Results always clamped at 0 (never negative)\n\n5. **Updated `invoiceTotals(invoice)`** to return:\n   - `subtotal`: sum of all line totals\n   - `discount`: sum of all line discounts\n   - `total`: subtotal - discount (clamped at 0, never negative)\n\n6. **Updated `renderInvoiceText(invoice)`** to display:\n   - Line items as before (qty, name, unit price, line total)\n   - If any discounts exist: Subtotal and Discount lines\n   - Final Total line\n\n**Tests added (25 new, 108 total passing):**\n- Discount validation (range, type, decimal values)\n- Discount calculations (single line, multiple lines, 100%)\n- Invoice totals with various discount scenarios\n- Rendering invoices with/without discounts\n- Zero-clamping enforcement",
